# The build context was 12GB, nearly all of it things the image must not have.
# Docker tars the whole context and hands it to the daemon before it reads the
# first instruction, so this is paid on every build, cached or not.

# UniRig's pixi environment: 11GB, built on first use, and pointless here.
.home/
# Generated assets, and the staging areas they pass through.
output/
input/
logs/
# The node packs are CLONED in the Dockerfile at pinned commits now, not
# copied from the host. Copying them would make the image depend on whatever
# state this particular machine's checkout happens to be in.
custom_nodes/
# ComfyUI's own user dir: its database, its logs, the Manager's cache. The two
# things in there we want are named explicitly by the Dockerfile
# (workflows/api and workflows/default/workflows), so the rest can go.
workflows/comfyui.db*
workflows/__manager/
workflows/*.log
# Host-specific, and secret-adjacent.
.env
*.log
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.git/
